From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alp Lab AB <contact@alplab.ai>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] sim: add a no-explicit-erase device regression test for the
 scratch trailer fix (#1066)

Companion to 0004-scramble-scratch-trailer-and-backward-scramble-off-by-
one.patch: adds scratch_trailer_cleared_after_swap to the mcuboot host
simulator (sim/, cargo + a C compiler, no embedded toolchain), which runs
a real, uninterrupted, permanent upgrade to completion on a flash device
that does not require an explicit erase before rewrite and asserts the
scratch area's temporary trailer never reads back as a GOOD magic
afterwards.

Getting there needed two pieces of new plumbing the simulator did not
have before, both additive and both defaulting to today's behaviour for
every existing test:

  * device_requires_erase(fa) (bootutil_area.h) is gated on
    MCUBOOT_SUPPORT_DEV_WITHOUT_ERASE / _WITH_ERASE. The simulator's own
    mcuboot_config.h never defined either, so every device the simulator
    ever built hardcoded device_requires_erase() == true regardless of
    erased_val -- the no-explicit-erase mechanism 0004 closes was
    unreachable by ANY sim test, not just an untested one. build.rs now
    defines both unconditionally, which switches the macro from a
    compile-time constant to the real runtime dispatch
    (flash_area_erase_required(), added to
    csupport/flash_map_backend/flash_map_backend.h), backed by a new
    SimFlash::erase_required (default true) plumbed through to C via
    sim_flash_erase_required() (mcuboot-sys/src/api.rs) the same way
    align/erased_val already are. A test opts a device out with the new
    SimFlash::set_erase_required(false), mirroring the existing
    set_verify_writes(false) escape hatch swap_size_erased_collision
    already uses for the same MRAM-is-directly-rewritable reason.

  * The STATE_0 branch 0004(i) fixes is itself gated on
    `!bs->use_scratch`, which requires the swapped image to NOT reach the
    trailer-holding sector(s) at the top of the slot -- slot >> image,
    matching AEN's real 2.75 MB slot against a far smaller application.
    make_image() (the maker every other sim_test! in this file uses)
    cannot produce that: maximal() ignores its size argument and always
    returns ImageSize::Largest, so every existing image fills its slot to
    capacity and use_scratch is always true -- verified empirically, zero
    `swap_scramble_trailer_sectors: fa_id=<scratch>` log lines across all
    26 device/align/erased_val combinations with make_image(). Added
    ImagesBuilder::make_image_undersized(), a small, self-contained maker
    that calls install_image() directly with ImageSize::Given(4096)
    instead of maximal(), touching no other maker or test.

Verified against the pinned upstream mcuboot revision
(6d3b3d2c38ab20c242e5b9abb04d050086383eb2, cargo 1.86.0 / gcc 13.3.0 on
WSL Ubuntu 24.04, ext/mbedtls submodule fetched at its pinned commit
2ca6c285a0dd3f33982dd57299012dacab1ff206), 0001-0003 applied first:

  * Pre-0004: the new test fails on the very first device/align/
    erased_val combination it tries -- the scratch area's temporary
    trailer reads back with a GOOD magic after a completed swap, exactly
    the self-perpetuating re-swap #1066 reported.
  * Post-0004: `cargo test --release --test core` -- 27 passed, 0 failed
    (26 pre-existing cases plus this one), across every device/alignment/
    erased_val {0x00, 0xff} combination each_device() sweeps.

Not wired into alp-sdk's own CI, for the same reason 0003 is not: needs a
Rust + C toolchain plus the ext/mbedtls submodule provisioned for the
vendored mcuboot checkout, a separate out-of-scope change. Reproduce
manually: `cd bootloader/mcuboot/sim && cargo test --release --test core
-- scratch_trailer_cleared_after_swap`. Upstream to mcu-tools/mcuboot
then drop alongside 0004.

Signed-off-by: Alp Lab AB <contact@alplab.ai>
---
diff --git a/sim/mcuboot-sys/build.rs b/sim/mcuboot-sys/build.rs
index 727f44f..1afc66a 100644
--- a/sim/mcuboot-sys/build.rs
+++ b/sim/mcuboot-sys/build.rs
@@ -48,6 +48,18 @@ fn main() {
     conf.conf.define("MCUBOOT_USE_FLASH_AREA_GET_SECTORS", None);
     conf.conf.define("MCUBOOT_HAVE_ASSERT_H", None);
     conf.conf.define("MCUBOOT_MAX_IMG_SECTORS", Some("128"));
+    // (alp-sdk#1066) Both, unconditionally: bootutil_area.h's
+    // device_requires_erase(fa) only compiles to the real runtime check
+    // (flash_area_erase_required(), csupport/flash_map_backend.h) when
+    // BOTH are defined; defining only _WITHOUT_ERASE would instead make
+    // every device in this build hardcode "never requires erase",
+    // silently changing all 26 pre-existing test cases instead of adding
+    // to them. flash_area_erase_required() itself defaults every device to
+    // "requires erase" (sim_flash_erase_required() in src/api.rs), so nothing
+    // observes a behaviour change unless a test opts a device out via
+    // SimFlash::set_erase_required(false).
+    conf.conf.define("MCUBOOT_SUPPORT_DEV_WITHOUT_ERASE", None);
+    conf.conf.define("MCUBOOT_SUPPORT_DEV_WITH_ERASE", None);
 
     if max_align_32 {
         conf.conf.define("MCUBOOT_BOOT_MAX_ALIGN", Some("32"));
diff --git a/sim/mcuboot-sys/csupport/flash_map_backend/flash_map_backend.h b/sim/mcuboot-sys/csupport/flash_map_backend/flash_map_backend.h
